# E2E fixtures. The temporal-worker entrypoint installs anything found in
# /app/e2e/fixtures/ as a plugin (when ARK_E2E_MODE=1); leaving them out of
# prod build contexts is defense-in-depth so an image built without the
# ARK_E2E_MODE gate still can't shadow the real claude-code executor.
# The e2e docker-compose bind-mounts ../e2e/fixtures into the container at
# runtime so tests still see them.
#
# NB: NOT excluding **/__tests__/ or *.test.ts -- packages/core/services/
# actions/index.ts imports ./__tests__/flaky-pr-fixture.js as part of the
# ARK_ENABLE_TEST_ACTIONS=1 path. Pre-rolled images saw `Cannot find
# module './__tests__/flaky-pr-fixture.js'` and crashlooped.
e2e/
